/lang/backend/mir

_ ascii-flag U32 = 1
_ valid-utf8-flag U32 = 2

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ StringHeader is Tuple

` What the header of a String says of its bytes, as `BxString.h` lays it out. The length in
` bytes is that of the span.

+ character-length U32
+ flags U32

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ do measure-string StringHeader
    - bytes ByteSpan

` The header of UTF-8 bytes, from one pass over them.
. characters U32
. flags = valid-utf8-flag /or/ ascii-flag
for index in 0 .. < bytes.length
    . byte = bytes.data[index]
    if byte >= 128
        flags = valid-utf8-flag
    if byte < 128 || byte >= 192
        characters += 1
= StringHeader(characters, flags)
